---
code: munge-name-invalid
when-fires: an emitted `<munged>__<role>` funcname is not a legal sh NAME (leading digit, dot, non-ASCII). oracle/reserved.rs lint_oracle_reserved_names.
why: ca-munge-charclass (24M §4b): a broken function name cannot ship — REFUSED. `{problem}` is `ShNameProblem::describe()`.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- munge-name-invalid && mise run loom:promote -- munge-name-invalid`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all munge-name-invalid` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
中pkg__predict() { :; }

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  error[munge-name-invalid]: sm `\xc3\xa4\xc2\xb8\xc2\xadpkg` munges to the sh
  function name `\xc3\xa4\xc2\xb8\xc2\xadpkg__predict`, which is not a legal
  NAME: non-ASCII character `\xc3\xa4` (a NAME admits only ASCII
  letters/digits/`_`) (ca-munge-charclass, 24M section 4b) -- REFUSED (a broken
  function name cannot ship; the munger must transliterate or the name must be
  renamed)
